SQL Practice Question

Problem Statement:
The sales team wants to identify customers whose total spending across all their orders is greater than 500. Use a subquery with an aggregate function to identify these customers. Then, display all orders placed by the identified customers.

Tables:

Customers

customer_id

customer_name


Orders

order_id

customer_id

order_date

order_amount


Query to be Implemented:
Write an SQL query to return:

customer_name

order_date

order_amount


Requirements:

Use the Customers and Orders tables.

Join the tables using customer_id.

Use one subquery.

Use an aggregate function such as SUM() to calculate each customer's total spending.

Use HAVING to identify customers whose total spending is greater than 500.

Display all orders placed by the identified customers.


Sample Data

customer_id	customer_name

1	Alice
2	Bob
3	Charlie


order_id	customer_id	order_date	order_amount

101	1	2024-04-01	150.00
102	1	2024-04-05	200.00
103	2	2024-04-02	300.00
104	2	2024-04-07	250.00
105	3	2024-04-03	100.00


Expected Output:

customer_name	order_date	order_amount

Bob	2024-04-02	300.00
Bob	2024-04-07	250.00


Your task: Write the SQL query.
